;; The tests bin/clojure-tests --aot --essential skips beyond the reference's :skipped-tests
;; (doc/FULL-SUPPORT-SURVEY.md, RPS74 (b), "As built: REAP8"): {NS {TEST REASON}}, overlaid on
;; test/arbace-go-aot-results.edn for the essential gate's subset only; the whole --aot (bin/gate
;; --full's suite-aot) still runs them (RPS43 (a)). The subset's reference is the AOT reference with
;; these tests skipped: the namespace's :test less one per test and the test's :failing entry gone,
;; its :pass unchanged, so a test here must make no assertion when it passes (one that does shows as
;; a regression of the subset). Read with the Clojure reader.
{clojure.test-clojure.transducers
 {seq-and-transducer "200,000 test.check trials (75 s of the subset's runs, the cached gate's longest new part; its is runs only on a failure): the whole --aot runs it (RPS74 (b), RPS43 (a))"}}
